WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
with everything going on,

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
sometimes we don't get
the details about everything,

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.238
and there's been a lot of talk
lately about 3-D printed guns,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
which if you don't know,
are guns that people

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
print themselves at home
using a 3-D printer.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.579 line:92%
But the technology and the laws

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.180 size:81% position:41%
surrounding those guns
are pretty confusing.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.151
Luckily, I saw a commercial
last night that explains it all.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:19.552 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Take a look.

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.054 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh! Gin!

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I enjoy
our little get-togethers.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know what
I don't enjoy?

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:27.627 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What?

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not feeling safe
in my own home.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:31.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's the state
of the world today.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.565 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Anything could happen.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.968 size:81% position:41%
-That's why I'm gonna
do something about it.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:35.735 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-What's that?

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.304 line:92%
-I'm gonna print my own 3-D gun.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.873 line:92%
-Well, that sounds interesting.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait.
How do you print a gun?

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:43.443 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's simple.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
A 3-D printer
liquefies thermoplastics

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.480 size:78% position:39%
and then lays it down
in a successive layer

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.885
in a specific pattern dictated
by the object you want to print.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.253 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-That does sound simple.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No, it doesn't.

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.989
-And you know you can trust
a 3-D printer to make a gun

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:59.125
because look what a good job
it did on this coffee mug.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:03.663
-Oh. Now, how much does one of
these 3-D printers cost, anyway?

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:04.697 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Are they expensive?

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.000 line:92%
-No, they're very affordable.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yes.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:11.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
They range anywhere
from $800 to $10,000.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:12.639 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-That is affordable.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:15.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you serious?
A real gun costs like $100.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But if you're printing a gun,
you're gonna want to go

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a more expensive
3-D printer.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:20.346 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Why?

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because if you don't make
the gun correctly...

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...it could break apart.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.517 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Then what?

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.886
-And then explode in your hands
when you fire it.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:27.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fun.
-Nope!

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, is printing a gun
even legal?

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, the federal government
passed a law

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.327
saying that it's legal
to post blueprints online

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
that tell you how to make
a 3-D gun, so yes.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then a federal judge
passed an injunction

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
saying you can't post
any more blueprints, so no.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.269
But no one said you have to
take down the blueprints

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are already online.
So who knows?

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that does sound
cut and dry.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That sounds
like an ethical minefield.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're funny.
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.748 size:81% position:41%
But, Barb, do you even
know how to use a gun?

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:56.583 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-How hard can it be?

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
I use a car every day,
and I didn't get

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:01.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
any special training
for that or even a license.

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You don't have a license?!
-No.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.724 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-We carpool to work!

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.192 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-You two gals have jobs?

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.627 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-This is very dangerous.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not as dangerous
as not having a gun.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:13.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have a gun.
I keep it right here in --

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh-oh.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.469 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, well.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.937 line:92%
-I swear to God, Margaret.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:21.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, Barb,
this is a terrible idea.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.675 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Please don't do this.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Too late.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.913 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Printing ]

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh. Is there
a Mrs. 3-D printer?

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.553
I'll have my very own gun
in just 37 short hours.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:37.524
That's enough time to beat
you two in another game of gin.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:43.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh!
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:47.600
-This message brought to you
by Big Bob's Gun &amp; Knife Show!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.704
Get a gun in five minutes
or less -- guaranteed!

